# `@: size_t p @w 3`, a primitive pointer: a reference declaration whose candidate is one value and one more is
# refused at the extra value, whether or not anything reads the name (DECLARATION-CANDIDATE-ROLE, steps/defects.md).
# It was taken for a machine local with the model; its L1 joined the 3 to the cell (`(cast: (@: size_t)
# l2_q0_from[0])3`).
fn: check () int
    size_t: w 1U
    @: size_t p @w 3
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
